  annote  = {Opened 2026-11-09 (arXiv abstract; the full text of arXiv:0710.4290 was opened in the independent check, same day). Their eq. 2 writes the dissipation of a system driven between equilibrium states as a relative entropy of forward and backward path probabilities, and their eq. 8 states that a relative entropy computed from partial information is a lower bound. The setting is driven, not stationary. The journal reference was not verified in this run and is omitted.}
}

